{"t": 400.61, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 2, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "HalfBridge_SSHI_Clamp", "rationale": "The previous SSHI_Bridge_Clamp is very close but fails on startup (too slow) and ripple (slightly too high). Startup is limited by the two-diode drop (0.5V) in the full bridge and the storage capacitor size. By moving to a half-bridge rectifier (D1, D2), we reduce the diode drop to 0.25V. Because the SSHI flip (L1, S1) effectively makes the piezo voltage positive during both half-cycles, a half-bridge can extract most of the energy while speeding up the cold start. This efficiency gain allows us to use a slightly larger storage capacitor C1 to resolve the ripple issue on S3 without violating the startup time limit on S4.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "HalfBridge_SSHI_Clamp", "rationale": "The previous SSHI_Bridge_Clamp is very close but fails on startup (too slow) and ripple (slightly too high). Startup is limited by the two-diode drop (0.5V) in the full bridge and the storage capacitor size. By moving to a half-bridge rectifier (D1, D2), we reduce the diode drop to 0.25V. Because the SSHI flip (L1, S1) effectively makes the piezo voltage positive during both half-cycles, a half-bridge can extract most of the energy while speeding up the cold start. This efficiency gain allows us to use a slightly larger storage capacitor C1 to resolve the ripple issue on S3 without violating the startup time limit on S4.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.0047}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 3.4e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "out"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D5", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "out"], "model": "DZ33"}, {"id": "C1", "type": "C", "nodes": ["out", "0"], "value": 3.3e-06}]}}
