{"t": 788.61, "kind": "proposal", "iteration": 4, "k": 1, "move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_Bridge_PiFilter", "rationale": "The previous 'SSHI_Bridge_Clamp' design was very close, but failed on startup time (tup) for light/weak loads. Reducing C_out to speed up startup increases the voltage ripple (vpp), creating a trade-off. To break this, I am implementing a pi-filter (C-L-C) after the rectifier. C_in absorbs the high-current charge pulses from the SSHI bridge, while L_filt and C_out form a low-pass filter that provides a very smooth DC voltage to the load. This allows C_out to be small enough (e.g., 0.8-1.0 uF) to satisfy the tup < 0.15s requirement while keeping vpp < 20mV.", "circuit": {"move": "new_topology", "name": "SSHI_Bridge_PiFilter", "rationale": "The previous 'SSHI_Bridge_Clamp' design was very close, but failed on startup time (tup) for light/weak loads. Reducing C_out to speed up startup increases the voltage ripple (vpp), creating a trade-off. To break this, I am implementing a pi-filter (C-L-C) after the rectifier. C_in absorbs the high-current charge pulses from the SSHI bridge, while L_filt and C_out form a low-pass filter that provides a very smooth DC voltage to the load. This allows C_out to be small enough (e.g., 0.8-1.0 uF) to satisfy the tup < 0.15s requirement while keeping vpp < 20mV.", "done": false, "components": [{"id": "L1", "type": "L", "nodes": ["pzp", "n1"], "value": 0.0047}, {"id": "S1", "type": "S", "nodes": ["n1", "pzn"], "ctrl": "G1"}, {"id": "G1", "type": "SYNC", "ton": 3.4e-05, "phase": 0.0, "edges": "both"}, {"id": "D1", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzp", "n_in"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D2", "type": "D", "nodes": ["pzn", "n_in"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D3", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzp"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "D4", "type": "D", "nodes": ["0", "pzn"], "model": "DSCH"}, {"id": "Cin", "type": "C", "nodes": ["n_in", "0"], "value": 2.2e-06}, {"id": "Lfilt", "type": "L", "nodes": ["n_in", "out"], "value": 0.01}, {"id"